@ [canonical_uuid] 3482e2ce-817c-4788-b185-35adaad414f7

& [ConstructiveHemisphere]
  + seven ordered operations provide a concrete bridge from current published source identity to a future sealed build receipt
  + deterministic compilation on the target host makes Cantor itself the producer of the governed build work object

& [AdversarialHemisphere]
  + a plan can be mistaken for authority or smuggle command execution through free-form strings paths or arguments
  + host inspection time randomness ambient environment or mutable installation roots can defeat determinism and conservation
  + a verifier sharing unchecked compiler output can become circular evidence

& [Synthesis]
  + retain closed typed records bounded atoms empty grants exact denials explicit unresolved facts pure recompilation fresh processes and protected before-after audits
  + postpone every physical build capability to a separately sourced and signed successor
